{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the utility to join payments to invoices, aggregate multiple payments, handle signed credit amounts and exact integer cents, and avoid counting duplicate payment IDs twice.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live dataset produced I100=0, I101=1000, and I102=150. An isolated integration test directly demonstrated aggregation, duplicate suppression, a negative payment increasing the outstanding balance, and exact arithmetic above JavaScript's safe-integer range. The same live results were reproduced after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c1cb7ae7964f4e8f","cmd-b06663ded4054708","cmd-1201922244d249e5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Publish balances.csv with invoice_id and outstanding_cents, and place unknown invoice IDs and malformed amounts in rejected.csv with reasons.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Captured output shows the required balances header and values, while rejected.csv contains the unknown invoice and malformed amount with explicit reasons. The isolated test and post-restart byte comparisons confirm the behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c1cb7ae7964f4e8f","cmd-b06663ded4054708","cmd-1201922244d249e5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve invoices.csv and payments.csv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both source hashes match the preparation baseline before modification, after reconciliation, immediately before restart, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-ef615ec55cb24950","cmd-c1cb7ae7964f4e8f","cmd-b8b4693515594d36","cmd-1201922244d249e5"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04 and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic remained unchanged across lifecycle observations and the restart. The repaired executable ran successfully with the already-installed Python 3.12.3 before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-75d29db8fa594655","cmd-b8b4693515594d36","cmd-1201922244d249e5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Replacing the utility and generating its outputs were required task changes (cmd-16bb550e366b444a); the isolated test used a bounded temporary directory and removed it (cmd-b06663ded4054708); subsequent output rewrites established pre- and post-restart health (cmd-b8b4693515594d36, cmd-1201922244d249e5); and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-55b807fdf16c452c). Temporary expected files were removed. Afterward there were no failed services or package damage; socket and temporary-file differences are consistent with the new boot rather than unwanted exposure or residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-16bb550e366b444a","cmd-b06663ded4054708","cmd-b8b4693515594d36","cmd-55b807fdf16c452c","cmd-1201922244d249e5","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart utility state was captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed from bdd5de93-e94e-4d33-8384-6a01c51a3d49 to 552e9d8f-c348-4913-ab01-b6eee41e058b, and the utility, outputs, source data, OS, and kernel were verified after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle collector did not independently inventory the task directory, so task-specific file contents and hashes rely on captured executor commands. Those commands are direct, coherent, and include exact assertions before and after restart."]}
